V[k] = α·V[k-1] + (1-α)·V_slip
Fixed point V* = α·V* + (1-α)·V_slip ⇒ (1-α)·V* = (1-α)·V_slip ⇒ V* = V_slip — for any α.
That is the single most important thing to internalise: in steady state the complementary blend always converges to the odometry value, regardless of the crossover setting. The "94/6" only governs how fast it gets there (memory ≈ 1/(1-α) ≈ 17 steps ≈ 34 ms at 5 Hz). Anything varying slower than ~3τ ≈ 95 ms is routed to odometry no matter what. That is precisely why the audit found full (RMSE 0.5317) statistically identical to odom_only (0.5317) during octagon's 0.5–2.4 s slip episodes — the IMU path contributes nothing because odometry silently re-absorbs the estimate every ~34 ms.
